Playing a Monk in vanilla, I reached the castle without MR. A friendly
throne had allowed me to genocide demilich and master lich (but not lich);
knowing that (plain) lich can't summon nasties, I decided to risk the
castle battle and try to get to the /oW for my MR.

As a lich was working his way through the crowd, I decided to zap /oDeath
-- I first checked the monster spoiler, which says that (plain) lich has
base MR of 30 (and that MR is a percentage), and does not have "magic"
listed as one of his resistances. I therefore believed that 1-3 shots of
/oDeath would probably take him out before he reached me.

No dice; he got close enough to destroy a piece of armor. This was clearly
a mistake, and I shouldn't have waited for him to get that close. But then
I did some wizmode testing, and it seems that Death never works on him.

My question is: How would you know that from the monster spoilers (I'm
using the mon?-343.txt files and MonsterManual)? Is there something else
besides base MR that is at work here, allowing him to ignore Death? I'm
wondering what other creatures Death doesn't work on.

